## Principles — The Nextreme Signature (Unbound, but Not Unruly)

- **You decide — but you justify.** Every engine/style/layout choice ties to one sentence about content. “Why this <pattern>?” is answered, not shrugged.
- **Editable / vector over impressive.** A prettier raster is a failed artifact. If it can be native, it is.
- **Geometry / page-as-canvas is law.** A <artifact> without fixed slot widths or per-page fill will drift into overlap/holes the moment real content lands. Every shape/page declares bounds; validation proves it.
- **Theme indirection is fidelity.** <Example: `schemeClr` vs `srgbClr`> is the contract that makes a template recolourable — hard <literal> breaks it.
- **Ghost / budget first.** If the title story / page budget is weak, no amount of cards saves it.
- **No glitch is minor.** One overlapping card / one river / one white-border cover is a credibility leak. Zero is the bar.

